IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part2`
IMPORT `ea-part2-continuity`
IMPORT `ea-part3-salary`
IMPORT `ea-part4-hours`
IMPORT `ea-parts5to8`
IMPORT `ea-part9-maternity`
IMPORT `ea-part10-leave`
IMPORT `ea-part12-records`
IMPORT `ea-part12-retrenchment`
IMPORT `ea-retrenchment-reporting-notification`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 5 December 2025 -- THE EMPLOYER'S SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the employer -- an individual or a company that employs someone under
-- a contract of service, asking about one employment (or, for retrenchment
-- reporting, one exercise of giving notices).
--
-- This is the SECOND seat on this encoding, beside the employee's (ea-seat.l4),
-- under the ruling of 21 October 2026 on more than one seat. It phrases the
-- rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions an
-- employer asks: whom the Act covers, how much notice I must give or pay, when
-- I may dismiss or suspend, when I must pay and what I may deduct, the rest
-- days, overtime and leave I must give, maternity pay, the records and terms I
-- must give, retrenchment reporting, and what I can be penalised for.
--
-- Nothing here is new law. Both seat layers draw on the same rules, so where
-- they ask about the same facts they cannot disagree; the mirror cases in
-- ea-cases-seat-employer.l4 show it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS (21 October 2026). Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no,
-- numbers and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the employer
-- states, each with an @desc worded as the employer would be asked ("How many
-- complete months has this employee worked for you?"). The records the long
-- modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those
-- answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
-- A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed
-- placeholder, with a comment saying so. Fields a rule does read are always
-- asked, except the figures the Minister may substitute: the s 29 and s 30
-- proportions, the s 32 percentage, the s 35 salary thresholds and the s 95A
-- deadline are taken as the Act states them (the modules' own constants), so
-- a later Ministerial substitution would change these answers.
--
-- NAMES. Every name defined here begins "As the employer, " so that no name can
-- clash with ea-seat.l4's (which are the employee's "Am I ...", "Can my
-- employer ..."). The two layers import together without "multiple
-- definitions". The names built in each WHERE are local to their question.
--
-- Each question is published with @export so that it can be deployed and asked
-- from a form. Where the Act's answer turns on a judgment it hands to someone
-- else (the due inquiry, a reasonable excuse, the Commissioner's permission),
-- the existing modules take it as a fact, and so does this layer; see NOTES.md.
--
-- Questions an employer would ask that the modules do not decide are listed in
-- NOTES.md under "Seats", not answered here.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- the employer's questions`

§§ `Whom the Act covers, and which Parts apply`

-- s 2(1). "Employee": a person who has entered into or works under a contract
-- of service, but not a seafarer, a domestic worker, or a class the Minister
-- has declared not to be employees.
@export Is the person I employ an "employee" under the Act (s 2(1))?
GIVEN `works under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into, or do they work under, a contract of service with you?
      `is a seafarer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a seafarer?
      `is a domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a domestic worker?
      `is in a class the Minister has declared not to be employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person in a class the Minister has declared, by Gazette notification, not to be employees?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, is this person an employee under the Act` IF
    `is an employee for the purposes of the Act` `works under a contract of service` `is a seafarer` `is a domestic worker` `is in a class the Minister has declared not to be employees`

-- s 35 (the same words as s 33(1)). Part 4 -- rest days, hours of work,
-- overtime -- covers a "workman" (an employee doing mainly manual labour)
-- earning up to $4,500 a month, and any other employee, not a manager or
-- executive, earning up to $2,600 a month, basic salary only.
@export Must I apply the Part 4 rest day, hours and overtime rules to this employee (s 35)?
GIVEN `the employee is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee's work mainly manual labour (are they a "workman")?
      `the employee is a manager or executive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee in a managerial or executive position?
      `the employee's basic monthly salary` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the employee's basic monthly salary, leaving out overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, must I apply Part 4 to this employee` IF
    `this Part applies to the employee` `the employee as a worker` `the caps as the Act states them`
    WHERE
        `the employee as a worker` MEANS Worker WITH
            `is a workman` IS `the employee is a workman`
            `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS `the employee is a manager or executive`
            `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS `the employee's basic monthly salary`
        -- The thresholds are the Act's own ($4,500 and $2,600), not asked.

-- s 68(1)-(4). A "child" is a person under 15. A child must not be employed in
-- an industrial or non-industrial undertaking, except in a family-only
-- industrial undertaking, or in light work suited to the child's capacity in a
-- non-industrial undertaking from age 13 (a medical officer's certificate is
-- conclusive on suitability).
@export Would employing this child break the Act (s 68)?
GIVEN `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in completed years?
      `in an industrial undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you employ the child in an industrial undertaking?
      `in a non-industrial undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you employ the child in a non-industrial undertaking?
      `the undertaking employs only family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the industrial undertaking employ only members of the same family?
      `the work is light and suited to the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work light work suited to the child's capacity?
      `a medical officer certified the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a medical officer certified the work as suited to the child's capacity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, would employing this child break the Act` IF
    `employing this child contravenes section 68(1)` `the child as a worker`
    WHERE
        `the child as a worker` MEANS YoungWorker WITH
            `age in completed years` IS `the child's age`
            `employed in an industrial undertaking` IS `in an industrial undertaking`
            `employed in a non-industrial undertaking` IS `in a non-industrial undertaking`
            `the industrial undertaking employs only members of the same family` IS `the undertaking employs only family`
            `the work is light work suited to the child's capacity` IS `the work is light and suited to the child`
            `a medical officer has certified the work suited to the child's capacity` IS `a medical officer certified the work`
            -- Placeholder: the s 68(1) rule does not read this field (s 69 does).
            `the Minister has declared this an industrial undertaking in which a young person must not be employed` IS FALSE

§§ `Notice, and ending the contract`

-- ss 8, 10(2), 10(3). The notice is the same for both sides (s 10(2)): the
-- contract's figure, unless shorter than the Act's minimum for the length of
-- service (1 day under 26 weeks, 1 week to 2 years, 2 weeks to 5 years, 4
-- weeks from 5 years), in which case s 8 voids it and the minimum applies.
@export How many days of notice must I give to end this employee's contract (ss 8, 10(2), 10(3))?
GIVEN `the contract sets the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract say how much notice must be given?
      `the contract's notice in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' notice does the contract give? (0 if it says nothing)
      `employed 26 weeks or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 26 weeks or more?
      `employed 2 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 2 years or more?
      `employed 5 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 5 years or more?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how many days of notice must I give` IS
    `the notice period that governs, in days` `the contract's terms` `the employee's service`
    WHERE
        `the contract's terms` MEANS ContractTerms WITH
            `the contract makes provision for notice` IS `the contract sets the notice`
            `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS `the contract's notice in days`
            -- Placeholder: the notice period rule does not read this field.
            `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS TRUE
        `the employee's service` MEANS ServiceLength WITH
            `employed for 26 weeks or more` IS `employed 26 weeks or more`
            `employed for 2 years or more` IS `employed 2 years or more`
            `employed for 5 years or more` IS `employed 5 years or more`

-- s 11(1). "Salary in lieu of notice": either party may end the contract
-- without notice by paying the salary at the gross rate of pay (before
-- deductions) that would have accrued over the notice period.
@export How much must I pay in lieu of notice, in dollars (s 11(1))?
GIVEN `the contract sets the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract say how much notice must be given?
      `the contract's notice in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' notice does the contract give? (0 if it says nothing)
      `employed 26 weeks or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 26 weeks or more?
      `employed 2 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 2 years or more?
      `employed 5 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 5 years or more?
      `the employee's gross daily pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the employee's gross pay for one day, before deductions, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how much must I pay in lieu of notice` IS
    `the payment in lieu of notice` `the employee's gross daily pay` `the contract's terms` `the employee's service`
    WHERE
        `the contract's terms` MEANS ContractTerms WITH
            `the contract makes provision for notice` IS `the contract sets the notice`
            `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS `the contract's notice in days`
            -- Placeholder: the payment in lieu rule does not read this field.
            `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS TRUE
        `the employee's service` MEANS ServiceLength WITH
            `employed for 26 weeks or more` IS `employed 26 weeks or more`
            `employed for 2 years or more` IS `employed 2 years or more`
            `employed for 5 years or more` IS `employed 5 years or more`

-- s 10(4), (5). The notice given is long enough if it is at least the period
-- that governs (the day of giving counts), or the other side waived notice.
@export Is the notice I have given long enough (s 10)?
GIVEN `the contract sets the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract say how much notice must be given?
      `the contract's notice in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' notice does the contract give? (0 if it says nothing)
      `employed 26 weeks or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 26 weeks or more?
      `employed 2 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 2 years or more?
      `employed 5 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this employee worked for you for 5 years or more?
      `days of notice I gave` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' notice did you give, counting the day you gave it?
      `the employee waived notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee waive their right to notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, is the notice I have given long enough` IF
    `the notice is long enough` `the notice I gave` `the contract's terms` `the employee's service`
    WHERE
        `the notice I gave` MEANS Notice WITH
            -- Placeholder: the "long enough" rule does not read this field
            -- (s 10(5), on writing, is a separate rule).
            `the notice is in writing` IS TRUE
            `the length given, in days` IS `days of notice I gave`
            `the receiving party waived the right to notice` IS `the employee waived notice`
        `the contract's terms` MEANS ContractTerms WITH
            `the contract makes provision for notice` IS `the contract sets the notice`
            `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS `the contract's notice in days`
            -- Placeholder: the "long enough" rule does not read this field.
            `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS TRUE
        `the employee's service` MEANS ServiceLength WITH
            `employed for 26 weeks or more` IS `employed 26 weeks or more`
            `employed for 2 years or more` IS `employed 2 years or more`
            `employed for 5 years or more` IS `employed 5 years or more`

-- s 11(2). Either party may end the contract without notice, and without
-- payment in lieu, on a "wilful breach" by the other party of a condition of
-- the contract.
@export May I end the contract without notice or payment because the employee wilfully broke a condition of it (s 11(2))?
GIVEN `there was a wilful breach by the other party of a condition of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee wilfully break a condition of the contract of service?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, may I end the contract without notice for the employee's wilful breach` IF
    `the party may terminate without notice and without payment under section 11(2)` `there was a wilful breach by the other party of a condition of the contract`

-- s 13(2). The employee is "deemed to have broken the contract" by being
-- absent for more than 2 days in a row without prior leave, with no
-- reasonable excuse or without telling (or trying to tell) the employer.
@export Is my employee treated as having broken the contract by being absent from work (s 13(2))?
GIVEN `days absent in a row` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in a row was the employee absent from work?
      `I gave leave beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the employee leave for the absence beforehand?
      `the employee had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee have a reasonable excuse for being absent?
      `the employee told me why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee tell you, or try to, why they were absent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, is my employee treated as having broken the contract by being absent` IF
    `the employee is deemed to have broken the contract` `the employee's absence`
    WHERE
        `the employee's absence` MEANS Absence WITH
            `days absent continuously` IS `days absent in a row`
            `with prior leave from the employer` IS `I gave leave beforehand`
            `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence` IS `the employee had a reasonable excuse`
            `the employee informed or attempted to inform the employer of the excuse` IS `the employee told me why`

-- s 13(1). The employer is deemed to have broken the contract if it fails to
-- pay salary in accordance with Part 3.
@export Am I treated as having broken the contract by failing to pay salary as Part 3 requires (s 13(1))?
GIVEN `the employer failed to pay salary in accordance with Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to pay salary as Part 3 requires (on time, in the right manner, without unauthorised deductions)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, am I treated as having broken the contract by not paying salary` IF
    `the employer is deemed to have broken the contract` `the employer failed to pay salary in accordance with Part 3`

-- s 15. The employee may leave without notice if they or their dependant are
-- immediately threatened with danger to the person by violence or disease that
-- the contract did not undertake.
@export May my employee leave without notice because of danger (s 15)?
GIVEN `the threat is to the employee or a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the danger to the employee, or to someone who depends on them?
      `the danger is immediate now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the danger immediate?
      `the danger is to the employee's person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a danger to the person (to body or life, not to property)?
      `the danger comes from violence or disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the danger come from violence or disease?
      `the contract made the employee run that risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee agree in the contract of service to run that risk?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, may my employee leave without notice because of danger` IF
    `the employee may terminate without notice under section 15` `the danger faced`
    WHERE
        `the danger faced` MEANS DangerFacts WITH
            `the threat is to the employee or the employee's dependant` IS `the threat is to the employee or a dependant`
            `the danger is immediate` IS `the danger is immediate now`
            `the danger is to the person` IS `the danger is to the employee's person`
            `the danger is by violence or disease` IS `the danger comes from violence or disease`
            `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run that risk` IS `the contract made the employee run that risk`

§§ `Dismissal and suspension`

-- s 14(1). After "due inquiry" (a proper inquiry into the alleged misconduct)
-- the employer may dismiss without notice for misconduct inconsistent with the
-- express or implied conditions of service.
@export May I dismiss this employee without notice for misconduct (s 14(1))?
GIVEN `the employee committed misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee commit misconduct that goes against the express or implied terms of the job?
      `I held a due inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you first hold a proper inquiry (a "due inquiry") into it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, may I dismiss without notice for misconduct` IF
    `the employer may dismiss without notice under section 14(1)` `the misconduct facts`
    WHERE
        `the misconduct facts` MEANS DismissalFacts WITH
            `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service` IS `the employee committed misconduct`
            `the employer held a due inquiry` IS `I held a due inquiry`
            -- Placeholders: the s 14(1) dismissal rule does not read these fields.
            `the employee was instead down-graded` IS FALSE
            `the employee was instead suspended without salary` IS FALSE
            `the days of suspension` IS 0

-- s 14(1)(b). Instead of dismissing, after the same due inquiry, the employer
-- may suspend without salary for no more than one week.
@export May I suspend this employee without pay (s 14(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the employee committed misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee commit misconduct that goes against the express or implied terms of the job?
      `I held a due inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you first hold a proper inquiry (a "due inquiry") into it?
      `I suspend without pay instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you suspending the employee without pay instead of dismissing them?
      `days of the suspension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the suspension last?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, may I suspend without pay` IF
    `the suspension is lawful under section 14(1)(b)` `the suspension facts`
    WHERE
        `the suspension facts` MEANS DismissalFacts WITH
            `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service` IS `the employee committed misconduct`
            `the employer held a due inquiry` IS `I held a due inquiry`
            -- Placeholder: the s 14(1)(b) suspension rule does not read this field.
            `the employee was instead down-graded` IS FALSE
            `the employee was instead suspended without salary` IS `I suspend without pay instead`
            `the days of suspension` IS `days of the suspension`

-- s 14(2A). Who may claim against the employer for wrongful dismissal: any
-- employee not a manager or executive; a manager or executive dismissed
-- without notice and without salary in lieu; or one dismissed with notice (or
-- salary in lieu) after 6 months' service.
@export Can the employee I dismissed claim against me for wrongful dismissal (s 14(2A))?
GIVEN `the employee was a manager or executive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employee in a managerial or executive position?
      `I dismissed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you dismiss the employee with notice?
      `I paid salary in lieu` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you dismiss the employee without notice but pay salary in place of notice?
      `the employee served 6 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the employee worked for you for at least 6 months, in any position?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, can the employee I dismissed claim for wrongful dismissal` IF
    `the employee may lodge a wrongful dismissal claim` `the dismissed employee`
    WHERE
        `the dismissed employee` MEANS Dismissed WITH
            `in a managerial or an executive position` IS `the employee was a manager or executive`
            `dismissed with notice` IS `I dismissed with notice`
            `dismissed without notice but paid salary in lieu` IS `I paid salary in lieu`
            `served that employer for at least 6 months in any position` IS `the employee served 6 months or more`

-- ss 18, 18A. A change of employer -- a statutory substitution, the employer's
-- death, a change of partners or trustees, or the transfer of an undertaking
-- -- does not break the continuity of the employee's service, which counts for
-- notice and for the benefit qualifying periods.
@export Does the change of employer keep the employee's period of service continuous (ss 18, 18A)?
GIVEN `a company was substituted by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a body corporate substituted as the employer by or under written law?
      `the employer died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employer die, with the employee taken on by the personal representatives or trustees?
      `the partners or trustees changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the employee?
      `an undertaking was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an undertaking, or part of one, transferred from one person to another?
      `the employee worked in the part transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee work for the transferor in the undertaking, or the part, that was transferred?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, is the employee's service continuous across the change of employer` IF
    `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` `the change of employer`
    WHERE
        `the change of employer` MEANS EmployerChange WITH
            `a body corporate was substituted as employer by or under written law` IS `a company was substituted by law`
            `the employer died and the employee was taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees` IS `the employer died`
            `there was a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person` IS `the partners or trustees changed`
            `an undertaking or part of one was transferred from one person to another` IS `an undertaking was transferred`
            `the employee was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS `the employee worked in the part transferred`

§§ `Paying salary`

-- ss 21 to 23. The time I have to pay: 7 days after the salary period for
-- ordinary salary, 14 for overtime, 3 days after a dismissal, on the day the
-- contract ends (on completion, or when the employee leaves with due notice),
-- and 7 days where the employee leaves without notice.
@export How many days do I have to pay this salary (ss 21 to 23)?
GIVEN `the occasion` IS A PaymentOccasion @desc What is the payment for?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how many days do I have to pay` IS
    `the number of days allowed for payment` `the occasion`

@export Did I pay late (ss 21 to 23)?
GIVEN `the occasion` IS A PaymentOccasion @desc What was the payment for?
      `the days taken to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the end of the salary period (or after the dismissal or the end of the contract) did you pay?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, did I pay late` IF
    `the payment was late` `the occasion` `the days taken to pay`

-- s 20A. For a monthly-rated employee who did not work the whole month
-- (started late, left early, unpaid leave, national service): monthly gross
-- rate divided by the days required to work, times the days worked, a day of
-- 5 hours or less counting as half.
@export How much salary must I pay for an incomplete month, in dollars (s 20A)?
GIVEN `the employee's monthly gross pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the employee's monthly gross rate of pay, in dollars?
      `full days required` IS A NUMBER @desc How many full days was the employee required to work that month?
      `short days required` IS A NUMBER @desc How many short days (5 hours or less) was the employee required to work that month?
      `full days worked` IS A NUMBER @desc How many full days did the employee actually work?
      `short days worked` IS A NUMBER @desc How many short days (5 hours or less) did the employee actually work?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how much salary must I pay for an incomplete month` IS
    `the salary due for the incomplete month` `the incomplete month`
    WHERE
        `the incomplete month` MEANS IncompleteMonth WITH
            -- Placeholders: the salary computation does not read these five
            -- fields (they decide whether s 20A applies, which is not asked).
            `the employee is monthly-rated` IS TRUE
            `commenced employment after the first day of the month` IS TRUE
            `employment was terminated before the end of the month` IS FALSE
            `took leave of absence without pay for one or more days` IS FALSE
            `took leave of absence to perform national service under the Enlistment Act 1970` IS FALSE
            `the monthly gross rate of pay` IS `the employee's monthly gross pay`
            `full days the employee is required to work in that month` IS `full days required`
            `short days the employee is required to work in that month, of 5 hours or less` IS `short days required`
            `full days actually worked` IS `full days worked`
            `short days actually worked, of 5 hours or less` IS `short days worked`

§§ `Deductions from salary`

-- ss 26, 27. No deduction unless the Act authorises it (or a court order or tax
-- recovery requires it). Deductions for accommodation, amenities and services,
-- cooperative society payments and any other deduction need the employee's
-- written consent, which the employee may withdraw before it is made.
@export May I make this deduction from the employee's salary (ss 26, 27)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DeductionKind @desc What is the deduction for?
      `the employee consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee give written consent to the deduction?
      `the employee withdrew consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee withdraw that consent in writing before the deduction was made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, may I make this deduction` IF
    `the deduction may lawfully be made` `the kind` `the employee's consent`
    WHERE
        `the employee's consent` MEANS Consent WITH
            `written consent was given` IS `the employee consented in writing`
            `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS `the employee withdrew consent in writing`

-- s 29. For damage or loss through the employee's neglect or default: no more
-- than the loss, no more than a quarter of one month's wages unless the
-- Commissioner for Labour permits more, and only after the employee has had a
-- chance to "show cause" (explain why it should not be made).
@export May I deduct this amount for damage or loss the employee caused (s 29)?
GIVEN `the loss the employee caused` IS A NUMBER @desc How much damage or loss did the employee's neglect or default cause, in dollars?
      `the employee's month's wages` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the employee's wages for one month, in dollars?
      `the amount I propose to deduct` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you propose to deduct, in dollars?
      `the Commissioner permitted a larger deduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner for Labour permitted a larger deduction?
      `the employee had a chance to show cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the employee a chance to explain why the deduction should not be made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, may I deduct this amount for damage or loss` IF
    `the damages deduction may be made` `the proposed damages deduction` `the proportions as the Act states them`
    WHERE
        `the proposed damages deduction` MEANS DamagesDeduction WITH
            `the amount of the damages or loss caused by the employee's neglect or default` IS `the loss the employee caused`
            `one month's wages` IS `the employee's month's wages`
            `the amount the employer proposes to deduct` IS `the amount I propose to deduct`
            `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction` IS `the Commissioner permitted a larger deduction`
            `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS `the employee had a chance to show cause`
        -- The proportion is the Act's own (one quarter), not asked.

-- s 28(2). A deduction for absence may not be a larger share of the salary for
-- the period than the time absent is of the time the employee was required to
-- work.
@export What is the most I may deduct for the employee's absence, in dollars (s 28(2))?
GIVEN `the salary for the period at the gross rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the employee's salary for the salary period at the gross rate of pay, in dollars?
      `the period for which the employee was absent` IS A NUMBER @desc How long was the employee absent (in days or hours)?
      `the total period the employee was required to work` IS A NUMBER @desc How long was the employee required to work in the salary period (in the same unit)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the most I may deduct for absence` IS
    `the maximum deduction for absence` `the salary for the period at the gross rate` `the period for which the employee was absent` `the total period the employee was required to work`

-- s 30(2). Deductions for accommodation, amenities and services: no more than
-- the value supplied, and in total no more than a quarter of the salary for
-- the salary period.
@export Are my deductions for accommodation, amenities and services within the limits (s 30)?
GIVEN `the total of such deductions in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of your deductions for accommodation, amenities and services this salary period, in dollars?
      `the value of what was supplied` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the accommodation, amenities or services you supplied, in dollars?
      `the salary payable for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the salary payable for the salary period, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, are my accommodation deductions within the limits` IF
    -- The proportion is the Act's own (one quarter), not asked.
    `the accommodation deductions are within section 30` `the total of such deductions in the period` `the value of what was supplied` `the salary payable for the period` `the proportions as the Act states them`

-- s 32. All deductions in a salary period, except for absence, recovery of
-- advances, loans and overpayments, and cooperative society payments, may not
-- exceed 50% of the salary for the period -- unless it is the last salary on
-- termination or completion.
@export Are my deductions this salary period within the 50% cap (s 32)?
GIVEN `the total of countable deductions in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of your deductions this salary period, leaving out those for absence, recovering advances, loans or overpayments, and cooperative society payments, in dollars?
      `the salary payable for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the salary payable for the salary period, in dollars?
      `this is the last salary on termination or completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the last salary, paid on termination or completion of the contract?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, are my deductions within the 50% cap` IF
    -- The percentage is the Act's own (50%), not asked.
    `the section 32 cap is satisfied` `the total of countable deductions in the period` `the salary payable for the period` `this is the last salary on termination or completion` `the proportions as the Act states them`

§§ `Rest days, hours and overtime`

-- s 36. Each week, one whole rest day without pay (Sunday or a day the
-- employer fixes), or for a shift worker a continuous 30 hours instead.
@export Have I allowed this employee a rest day this week (s 36)?
GIVEN `I allowed a whole rest day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you allow the employee one whole day of rest this week?
      `the employee does shift work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employee do shift work?
      `I gave 30 hours in a row instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give a continuous period of 30 hours off instead?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I allowed a rest day this week` IF
    `a rest day was allowed in the week` `the rest day arrangement`
    WHERE
        `the rest day arrangement` MEANS RestDayArrangement WITH
            `a rest day of one whole day was allowed in the week` IS `I allowed a whole rest day`
            `the employee is engaged in shift work` IS `the employee does shift work`
            `a continuous period of 30 hours was substituted` IS `I gave 30 hours in a row instead`
            -- Placeholders: the s 36 rest day rule does not read these fields.
            `the substituted period commenced before 6 p.m. on a Sunday` IS FALSE
            `the employer determines the rest day` IS FALSE
            `a roster was prepared before the commencement of the month` IS FALSE

-- s 37. What I must pay for work on the employee's rest day: half a day's, one
-- day's, or more pay depending on the hours, doubled where the work was at my
-- request, with hours beyond normal hours at one and a half times.
@export What must I pay for the employee's work on a rest day, in dollars (s 37)?
GIVEN `the employee asked to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee work on the rest day at their own request (rather than yours)?
      `hours worked on the rest day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did the employee work on the rest day?
      `usual hours were agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and the employee agreed their usual hours of work per day?
      `the agreed usual hours` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many hours a day? (0 if not agreed)
      `the employee's basic daily pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the employee's basic pay for one day's work, in dollars?
      `the employee's hourly basic pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the employee's basic pay per hour, without allowances, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, what must I pay for rest day work` IS
    `the payment for working on the rest day` `the rest day work done`
    WHERE
        `the rest day work done` MEANS RestDayWork WITH
            `hours agreed as the usual hours of work per day were agreed` IS `usual hours were agreed`
            `the agreed usual hours of work per day` IS `the agreed usual hours`
            `the hours actually worked on the rest day` IS `hours worked on the rest day`
            `the basic rate of pay for one day's work` IS `the employee's basic daily pay`
            `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS `the employee's hourly basic pay`
            `the work was at the employee's own request` IS `the employee asked to work`

-- s 38(4). Overtime at not less than one and a half times the "hourly basic
-- rate of pay" (basic pay, without allowances, per hour).
@export How much overtime must I pay, in dollars (s 38(4))?
GIVEN `the extra hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of overtime did the employee work?
      `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the employee's basic pay per hour, without allowances, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how much overtime must I pay` IS
    `the overtime payment` `the extra hours` `the hourly basic rate of pay`

-- s 38(1), (4). The hours in a day beyond the daily limit (8, or 9 where the
-- contract has shorter days elsewhere in the week or a 5-day week) are extra
-- work that attracts overtime.
@export How many of the employee's hours today must I pay as overtime (s 38(1), (4))?
GIVEN `hours worked today` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did the employee work today?
      `some days are shorter than 8 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed with the employee that they work less than 8 hours on one or more days of the week?
      `the employee works 5 days or fewer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed with the employee that they work no more than 5 days a week?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how many hours today attract overtime` IS
    `the daily hours attracting overtime` `the hours today`
    WHERE
        `the hours today` MEANS HoursWorked WITH
            `the pattern` IS WorkPattern WITH
                `by agreement, hours on one or more days of the week are less than 8` IS `some days are shorter than 8 hours`
                `by agreement, the employee works not more than 5 days a week` IS `the employee works 5 days or fewer`
                -- Placeholder: the daily ceiling does not read this field.
                `by agreement, hours in every alternate week are less than 44` IS FALSE
            `hours worked in the day` IS `hours worked today`
            -- Placeholders: the daily overtime rule does not read these fields.
            `hours worked in the week` IS 0
            `hours worked in the continuous period of 2 weeks` IS 0
            `consecutive hours worked without a period of leisure` IS 0
            `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 0
            `overtime hours worked in the month` IS 0
            `a section 38(2) circumstance applies` IS FALSE

-- s 38(1)(a). No more than 6 consecutive hours without a period of leisure.
@export Have I made the employee work more than 6 hours in a row without a break (s 38(1)(a))?
GIVEN `hours in a row without a break` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest the employee worked in a row without a break, in hours?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I broken the 6 consecutive hours rule` IF
    `section 38(1)(a) was contravened` `the hours without a break`
    WHERE
        `the hours without a break` MEANS HoursWorked WITH
            `consecutive hours worked without a period of leisure` IS `hours in a row without a break`
            -- Placeholders: the s 38(1)(a) rule does not read these fields.
            `the pattern` IS WorkPattern WITH
                `by agreement, hours on one or more days of the week are less than 8` IS FALSE
                `by agreement, the employee works not more than 5 days a week` IS FALSE
                `by agreement, hours in every alternate week are less than 44` IS FALSE
            `hours worked in the day` IS 0
            `hours worked in the week` IS 0
            `hours worked in the continuous period of 2 weeks` IS 0
            `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 0
            `overtime hours worked in the month` IS 0
            `a section 38(2) circumstance applies` IS FALSE

-- s 38(5). No more than 72 hours of overtime a month.
@export Have I let the employee work more than 72 hours of overtime this month (s 38(5))?
GIVEN `overtime hours this month` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of overtime has the employee worked this month?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I broken the 72 hour overtime limit` IF
    `section 38(5) was contravened` `the overtime this month`
    WHERE
        `the overtime this month` MEANS HoursWorked WITH
            `overtime hours worked in the month` IS `overtime hours this month`
            -- Placeholders: the s 38(5) rule does not read these fields.
            `the pattern` IS WorkPattern WITH
                `by agreement, hours on one or more days of the week are less than 8` IS FALSE
                `by agreement, the employee works not more than 5 days a week` IS FALSE
                `by agreement, hours in every alternate week are less than 44` IS FALSE
            `hours worked in the day` IS 0
            `hours worked in the week` IS 0
            `hours worked in the continuous period of 2 weeks` IS 0
            `consecutive hours worked without a period of leisure` IS 0
            `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 0
            `a section 38(2) circumstance applies` IS FALSE

§§ `Holidays and leave`

-- s 88. A paid holiday at the gross rate of pay on each public holiday during
-- the employment -- unless another day was substituted by agreement, the
-- employee is on unpaid leave at their own request, or the holiday fell on a
-- non-working day and I gave a day off instead.
@export Must I give the employee a paid holiday for this public holiday (s 88)?
GIVEN `it is a public holiday in the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a public holiday that falls during the employment?
      `the employee is on unpaid leave they asked for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee on unpaid leave that you granted at their request?
      `another day was agreed instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and the employee agree to substitute another day for the holiday?
      `it falls on a non-working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the holiday fall on a day the employee is not required to work?
      `I gave a day off instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the employee a day off in its place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, must I give a paid holiday` IF
    `the employee is entitled to a paid holiday` `the holiday facts`
    WHERE
        `the holiday facts` MEANS PublicHolidayFacts WITH
            `the day is a public holiday falling during the employment` IS `it is a public holiday in the employment`
            `another day was substituted by agreement` IS `another day was agreed instead`
            -- Placeholder: the s 88 entitlement rule does not read this field.
            `the public holiday falls on a rest day` IS FALSE
            `the public holiday falls on a day the employee is not required to work` IS `it falls on a non-working day`
            `the employee is on leave of absence without pay granted at the employee's request` IS `the employee is on unpaid leave they asked for`
            `the employer gave a day off in substitution` IS `I gave a day off instead`

-- s 88A. Paid "annual leave": 7 days in the first year of service, one more
-- day for each further year to 14; pro-rated in a part year; nothing under 3
-- months, and none where the employee was absent without permission or excuse
-- on more than 20% of working days.
@export How many days of paid annual leave must I give this employee this year (s 88A)?
GIVEN `complete months of service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months has this employee worked for you?
      `complete years of service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete years (12-month periods) of continuous service has the employee had with you?
      `complete months this year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months has the employee worked in this year of service?
      `absent on over 20% of days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employee absent without permission or reasonable excuse on more than 20% of their working days?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how many days of annual leave must I give` IS
    `the annual leave days the employee is entitled to` `the employee's leave service`
    WHERE
        `the employee's leave service` MEANS LeaveService WITH
            `completed months of service with the employer` IS `complete months of service`
            `completed 12 month periods of continuous service` IS `complete years of service`
            `completed months of service in that year` IS `complete months this year`
            `absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days` IS `absent on over 20% of days`

-- s 89. Paid sick leave after examination by a medical practitioner: up to 14
-- days of outpatient sick leave a year, or up to 60 where hospitalisation is
-- necessary, scaled down in the first 6 months.
@export How many days of paid sick leave must I allow this employee this year (s 89)?
GIVEN `complete months of service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months has this employee worked for you?
      `a doctor examined the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employee examined by a medical practitioner?
      `hospitalisation is needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is hospitalisation necessary?
      `days in hospital` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the employee hospitalised this year? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how many days of paid sick leave must I allow` IS
    `the paid sick leave ceiling in days` `the employee's sick leave facts`
    WHERE
        `the employee's sick leave facts` MEANS SickLeaveFacts WITH
            `completed months of service with the employer` IS `complete months of service`
            `examined by a medical practitioner` IS `a doctor examined the employee`
            `hospitalisation is necessary` IS `hospitalisation is needed`
            `days on which the employee is hospitalised` IS `days in hospital`

-- s 45. No retrenchment benefit is owed to an employee with less than 2 years'
-- continuous service dismissed for redundancy or reorganisation.
@export Does the Act bar any retrenchment benefit because the employee's service was too short (s 45)?
GIVEN `I dismissed for redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you dismiss the employee because of redundancy or a reorganisation of the business?
      `years of continuous service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of continuous service has the employee had with you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, does short service bar a retrenchment benefit` IF
    `section 45 bars any retrenchment benefit` `the employee's service for benefits`
    WHERE
        `the employee's service for benefits` MEANS ServiceForBenefits WITH
            `years of continuous service with the employer` IS `years of continuous service`
            `dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation` IS `I dismissed for redundancy`
            -- Placeholder: the s 45 rule does not read this field (s 46 does).
            `the service has ceased` IS TRUE

§§ `Maternity`

-- s 76(1A), (2B), s 83. I must pay the "benefit period" -- 8 weeks of the
-- maternity absence -- if she has served me at least 3 months before
-- confinement (giving birth) and has not worked for another employer during
-- the absence.
@export Must I pay this employee during her maternity benefit period (ss 76, 83)?
GIVEN `she delivered on or after 22 August 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the baby born (or is it expected) on or after 22 August 2015?
      `her months of service before confinement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months had she worked for you before the day she gave birth?
      `she worked for another employer during it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has she worked for another employer during her maternity absence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, must I pay during the maternity benefit period` IF
    `she is entitled to payment during the benefit period` `her maternity facts`
    WHERE
        `her maternity facts` MEANS MaternityFacts WITH
            -- Placeholder: the entitlement rule does not read this field.
            `the arrangement` IS `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after`
            `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day` IS `she delivered on or after 22 August 2015`
            `months served preceding the day of confinement` IS `her months of service before confinement`
            -- Placeholders: the entitlement rule does not read these fields.
            `the gross rate of pay for one day` IS 0
            `days worked during the benefit period before confinement` IS 0
            `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part` IS `she worked for another employer during it`

-- s 76(1A). The gross rate of pay for each day of the 8-week benefit period.
@export How much maternity pay must I pay, in dollars (s 76(1A))?
GIVEN `how she takes her absence` IS AN AbsenceArrangement @desc How is she taking her maternity absence?
      `she delivered on or after 22 August 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the baby born (or is it expected) on or after 22 August 2015?
      `her months of service before confinement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months had she worked for you before the day she gave birth?
      `her gross daily pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is her gross pay for one day, before deductions, in dollars?
      `she worked for another employer during it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has she worked for another employer during her maternity absence?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, how much maternity pay must I pay` IS
    `the payment for the benefit period` `her maternity facts`
    WHERE
        `her maternity facts` MEANS MaternityFacts WITH
            `the arrangement` IS `how she takes her absence`
            `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day` IS `she delivered on or after 22 August 2015`
            `months served preceding the day of confinement` IS `her months of service before confinement`
            `the gross rate of pay for one day` IS `her gross daily pay`
            -- Placeholder: the payment rule does not read this field.
            `days worked during the benefit period before confinement` IS 0
            `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part` IS `she worked for another employer during it`

-- s 81. While she is absent on maternity leave, I may not give notice of
-- dismissal during the absence, or on a day such that it would expire during
-- it.
@export Would my notice of dismissal around her maternity absence be unlawful (s 81)?
GIVEN `the employee is absent in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is she absent on maternity leave under Part 9 of the Act?
      `notice of dismissal was given during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you giving the notice of dismissal during that absence?
      `the notice would expire during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the notice run out during that absence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, would my notice of dismissal during her maternity absence be unlawful` IF
    `the notice of dismissal is unlawful under section 81` `the employee is absent in accordance with this Part` `notice of dismissal was given during the absence` `the notice would expire during the absence`

-- s 82. Knowingly employing her in the 4 weeks immediately after her
-- confinement is an offence.
@export Am I guilty of an offence for employing her in the 4 weeks after she gave birth (s 82)?
GIVEN `the employer employed her during the 4 weeks immediately following confinement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you employ her at any time in the 4 weeks immediately after she gave birth?
      `the employer knew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know you were doing so?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, am I guilty of the section 82 offence` IF
    `the employer is guilty of an offence under section 82` `the employer employed her during the 4 weeks immediately following confinement` `the employer knew`

§§ `Records, key employment terms and pay slips`

-- s 95(1), (3). I must make and keep, for the prescribed period, employee
-- records with the prescribed particulars for every employee and former
-- employee; an incomplete or inaccurate record is a failure whether or not I
-- knew.
@export Have I kept this employee's record as the Act requires (s 95(1), (3))?
GIVEN `I made a record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a record for this employee?
      `it has the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the record contain the prescribed particulars?
      `I kept it for the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you kept it for the whole prescribed retention period?
      `it is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record incomplete or inaccurate in any way?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I kept the employee record as required` IF
    `the employer has complied with section 95(1)` `the employee's record`
    WHERE
        `the employee's record` MEANS EmployeeRecord WITH
            -- Placeholder: the s 95(1) rule does not read this field.
            `the person is an employee or a former employee of the employer` IS TRUE
            `a record was made` IS `I made a record`
            `the record contains the prescribed particulars` IS `it has the prescribed particulars`
            `the record has been kept throughout the prescribed record retention period` IS `I kept it for the prescribed period`
            -- Placeholder: the s 95(1) rule does not read this field (s 95(2) does).
            `the record is readily accessible to the employee or former employee` IS TRUE
            `the record is incomplete or inaccurate` IS `it is incomplete or inaccurate`
            -- Placeholder: the s 95(1) rule does not read this field; by
            -- s 95(3) knowledge does not matter.
            `the employer knew it was incomplete or inaccurate` IS FALSE

-- s 95A. "Key employment terms": the written record of the main terms of the
-- job, due within 14 days of the start of employment, for contracts made on or
-- after 1 April 2016 and service of at least the prescribed minimum.
@export Have I failed to give the employee the written key employment terms in time (s 95A)?
GIVEN `the contract was made after 1 April 2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee enter into the contract of service on or after 1 April 2016?
      `employed for the prescribed minimum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee employed for at least the prescribed minimum period of service?
      `I gave the key terms in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the employee the key employment terms in writing?
      `days after the start I gave them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the employee started work did you give them? (0 if never)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I failed to give the key employment terms in time` IF
    `the employer has contravened section 95A` `the key terms facts`
    WHERE
        `the key terms facts` MEANS KeyTermsFacts WITH
            `the contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016` IS `the contract was made after 1 April 2016`
            `employed for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service` IS `employed for the prescribed minimum`
            `a written record of the key employment terms was given` IS `I gave the key terms in writing`
            `days after the start of employment when it was given` IS `days after the start I gave them`
            -- The seat assumes the Act's own figure: no other deadline is
            -- prescribed, so the 14 days in s 95A(2) govern.
            `another period has been prescribed in substitution` IS FALSE
            `the substituted period in days` IS 0

-- s 96. A pay slip (paper or an electronic record the employee can keep) for
-- each salary period and for any sum paid on dismissal or termination, in time,
-- in the prescribed form, complete and accurate -- unless exempted.
@export Have I met the pay slip duty (s 96)?
GIVEN `I gave a pay slip for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the employee a pay slip for the salary period?
      `I gave it electronically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it as an electronic record the employee can access and keep for later reference?
      `I gave it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it within the prescribed time?
      `it is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in the prescribed form, with the prescribed information?
      `the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the pay slip incomplete or inaccurate in any way?
      `I paid a sum on dismissal or termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the employee a sum on dismissal or termination (under s 22 or 23)?
      `I gave a pay slip for that sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give a pay slip for that sum?
      `I am exempted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempted by an order under s 96(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I met the pay slip duty` IF
    `the employer has complied with section 96` `the pay slip facts`
    WHERE
        `the pay slip facts` MEANS PaySlipFacts WITH
            `a pay slip was given for the salary period` IS `I gave a pay slip for the period`
            `a pay slip was given for a sum paid under section 22 or 23` IS `I gave a pay slip for that sum`
            `a sum was paid under section 22 or 23` IS `I paid a sum on dismissal or termination`
            `given within the time prescribed` IS `I gave it in time`
            `in the prescribed form and containing the prescribed information` IS `it is in the prescribed form`
            `given as an electronic record accessible and useable for subsequent reference` IS `I gave it electronically`
            `the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate` IS `the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate`
            `the employer is exempted by an order under section 96(5)` IS `I am exempted`

§§ `Retrenchment reporting`

-- s 96A and the Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019, para 3.
-- An employer with 10 or more covered employees on the day it gives a covered
-- employee (open-ended contract, or a term of at least 6 months) notice of
-- "retrenchment" (ending the contract at the employer's initiative for
-- redundancy or reorganisation) must report it to the Commissioner for Labour.
@export Must I report this retrenchment to the Commissioner for Labour (s 96A; Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, para 3)?
GIVEN `the person is an employee under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an "employee" under the Act (working under a contract of service, and not a seafarer or domestic worker)?
      `the contract has an end date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employee's contract of service say when it ends?
      `the contract's term in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months is it for? (0 if open-ended)
      `my covered employees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees covered by the Notification did you have on the day you gave notice?
      `I ended the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it you who decided to end the employment?
      `the reason is redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reason redundancy or a reorganisation of your business?
      `the day I gave notice` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did you give notice, as a day number (day 0 is Monday 1 November 2021)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, must I report this retrenchment` IF
    `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` `the notice I gave of retrenchment`
    WHERE
        `the notice I gave of retrenchment` MEANS `Notice of retrenchment` WITH
            `the person is an employee under section 2(1) of the Act` IS `the person is an employee under the Act`
            `the contract` IS `Contract of service` WITH
                `specifies an end date` IS `the contract has an end date`
                `term of employment in months` IS `the contract's term in months`
            `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` IS `my covered employees`
            `the employer initiated the termination` IS `I ended the employment`
            `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation` IS `the reason is redundancy`
            `the day the notice is given` IS `the day I gave notice`
            -- Placeholder: the para 3 duty does not read this field.
            `the day the notice takes effect` IS `the day I gave notice`

-- Notification para 4. The report is due no later than 5 working days (not a
-- Saturday, Sunday or public holiday) after the day the notice is given. Days
-- are day numbers: day 0 is Monday 1 November 2021.
@export What is the last day for my retrenchment report, as a day number (Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, para 4)?
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did you give the notice of retrenchment, as a day number (day 0 is Monday 1 November 2021)?
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc Which days in the period are public holidays, as day numbers?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the last day for my retrenchment report` IS
    `the last day for the retrenchment report` `the day the notice is given` `public holidays`

-- s 96A(2) with the Notification. Compliance is counted employee by employee:
-- every notice needing a report must be reported in time, in the form, with
-- every particular.
@export Have I complied with the retrenchment reporting duty (s 96A(2))?
GIVEN `covered employees on the day notice is given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many covered employees did you have on the day the notice was given?
      `notices needing a report` IS A NUMBER @desc How many notices of retrenchment did you give that need a report?
      `notices reported in time, in form and with every particular` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those did you report in time, in the required form and with every particular?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I complied with retrenchment reporting` IF
    `the employer has complied with section 96A(2)` (`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` `covered employees on the day notice is given` `notices needing a report` `notices reported in time, in form and with every particular`)

§§ `What I can be penalised for`

-- ss 126A(aa), 126B(1)(aa). Each retrenched employee not properly reported is
-- one occasion for an administrative penalty of the prescribed amount; the
-- officer "may" issue a notice, so this is the most the penalties could total.
-- The prescribed amount is not in the Act and is supplied.
@export What is the most my administrative penalties for retrenchment reporting could total, in dollars (ss 126A, 126B)?
GIVEN `covered employees on the day notice is given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many covered employees did you have on the day the notice was given?
      `notices needing a report` IS A NUMBER @desc How many notices of retrenchment did you give that need a report?
      `notices reported in time, in form and with every particular` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those did you report in time, in the required form and with every particular?
      `the prescribed amount per occasion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed administrative penalty for each occasion, in dollars? (Set by regulations, not the Act.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the most my retrenchment reporting penalties could total` IS
    `the most the administrative penalties could total` (`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` `covered employees on the day notice is given` `notices needing a report` `notices reported in time, in form and with every particular`) `the prescribed amount per occasion`

-- s 126D(2). Failing, without reasonable excuse, to comply with an authorised
-- officer's direction to end or remedy a civil contravention is an offence.
@export Have I committed the offence of not complying with a direction (s 126D(2))?
GIVEN `a direction was given under section 126D(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an authorised officer give you a direction under s 126D(1)?
      `the employer failed to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with it?
      `the employer had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the employer, have I committed the section 126D(2) offence` IF
    `the employer has committed the section 126D(2) offence` `a direction was given under section 126D(1)` `the employer failed to comply with it` `the employer had a reasonable excuse`

-- s 126D(2): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 6 months or ... both".
@export What is the most I can be fined for not complying with a direction, in dollars (s 126D(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the most I can be fined for disobeying a direction` IS
    `the maximum fine for disobeying a section 126D direction`

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for not complying with a direction, in months (s 126D(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As the employer, what is the longest I can be imprisoned for disobeying a direction` IS
    `the maximum imprisonment in months for disobeying a section 126D direction`
